text:
Alex W: quick check — running into 401s on long-lived streaming connections when using a cross-project service account impersonation flow in the Node SDK. Any known gotchas?
Maya R: do you mean using a local key to impersonate a SA in a different project, then opening multiple streams concurrently?
Alex W: yep — we create an access token via our token-exchange helper, then pass that to client.stream(). After ~15m some streams get 401 and reconnect, others keep going. looks like racey refresh?
Liam C: sounds like refresh contention. are you doing refresh per-stream or a shared refresh cache?
Alex W: per-stream right now. simplest fix was to reduce concurrent refreshes but we need a cleaner fix.
Maya R: recommended: centralize token refresh per service-account + target-project. single refresher with mutex + short memcache TTL. SDK should expose a tokenProvider hook for this.
Maya R: example pattern in Node (very basic):
```
// pseudocode
const cache = new Map();
async function getToken(saKeyPath, targetProj) {
  const key = `${saKeyPath}|${targetProj}`;
  if (cache.has(key) && cache.get(key).expiry > Date.now()) return cache.get(key).token;
  // mutex per-key
  await lockFor(key);
  try {
    // double-check after acquiring lock
    if (cache.has(key) && cache.get(key).expiry > Date.now()) return cache.get(key).token;
    const token = await exchangeJwtForAccessToken(saKeyPath, {targetProject});
    cache.set(key, {token, expiry: Date.now() + (token.expires_in - 30) * 1000});
    return token;
  } finally { unlockFor(key) }
}
client.stream({ auth: () => getToken('/creds/impersonator.json','proj-b') })
```
Priya S: also check the AUD/target_audience when doing an OIDC-style exchange — if the audience isn't the token endpoint or the Redwood token-audience we expect, implicit rejection can happen after refresh.
Alex W: good call — I had omitted the target_audience and a few invalid auds were returned from our idp.
Liam C: other thing: tune streaming reconnect backoff. default in SDK is expo jitter but some users open 50+ streams — we throttle reconnects server-side and if many clients retry at once you see a cascade of 401s as servers rotate ephemeral keys.
Maya R: config we use in prod:
```
stream.retry = { baseMs: 250, maxMs: 60000, factor: 1.6, jitter: 0.25, maxAttempts: 12 }
```
Maya R: plus add a random start jitter per stream (0-300ms) so they don't align.
Alex W: thanks — will centralize refresh + set target_audience + random jitter. any doc links I should read?
DevEx Bot: shared resource: https://redwood.internal/devex/auth/service-accounts — sections: "impersonation cache pattern" and "streaming backoff recommendations" :book:
Priya S: if you want I can open a tiny PR to expose tokenProvider in the Node SDK (small change) and add a sample in examples/auth.
Alex W: please do, that'd save us time. tagging you @Priya S :thumbsup:
